mdv: "1.0"
title: Availability against the objective
---

# Availability against the objective

A gauge is a one-number form, so this is one number: the quarter's attainment,
sat in the band it landed in. The range is declared rather than derived, because
an availability gauge scaled to its own data would put 99.94 halfway up an arc
and say nothing about the objective it is being measured against.

```mdv gauge
title: Availability, FY26 Q2 (%)
value: attainment
min: 99
max: 100
showValue: true
thresholds:
  - {at: 99, status: critical, label: Breaching}
  - {at: 99.5, status: warning, label: At risk}
  - {at: 99.9, status: good, label: Meeting objective}
format: table
---
attainment
99.94
```
